{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208651-elemental-associations-for-single-point-style-charms","id":1208651,"title":"Elemental Associations for Single Point Style Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-18T18:21:09-07:00","id":1208651,"title":"Elemental Associations for Single Point Style Charms","content":"There's a weapon in <i>RWBY</i> which is basically a reaper daiklave with a mechanical, rotating sheath containing a number of interchangeable magical blades of different colors and elemental powers.<br /> <br /> hose powers are most dramatic when one of the blades is shattered. Replacing a broken blade might require a new supply of jade and a major crafting project rather than a major or superior repair project. As an artifact weapon in Creation, the sheath might contain as many as ten blades; two for each color of jade.<br /> <br /> As a reaper daiklave with a strong incentive to constantly sheath and draw the sword to exchange one blade for an unbroken edge or a different element, naturally its Evocations could lend themselves to Single Point Shining into the Void.<br /> <br /> Single Point is a rather Willpower-expensive Style; with the exception of the pinnacle Charm, all of its post-Form Charms cost a Willpower point. Perhaps a stylist (of any Exaltation) with this weapon can shatter an appropriate blade after using an appropriate one of those Charms?<br /> <br /> <br /> Void-Slicing Wind is an easy match to the blue jade Air blades.<br /> <br /> Liquid Steel Flow is an acceptable match to the black jade Water blades.<br /> <br /> Six-Demon Scabbard Binding seems perfect for the white jade Earth blades.<br /> <br /> Fatal Stroke Flash could be Fire?<br /> <br /> Horizon-Swallowed Star Flash might be Wood?<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded-specific Evocations ideas include letting a Prince of the Earth:<br /> <br /> * treat drawing one of the sword's blades as an opportunity to activate Dragon-Graced Weapon, granting the blade the blessing of its associated element, and making it just a little easier for the Prince of the Earth to enter the specific Aura she desires.<br /> <br /> * shatter in place of the Willpower cost of appropriate Melee Charms (especially the Signature ones), if the blade's color matches the Charm's element. In the case of scene-long Aura of Grasping Branches, the green jade blade would remain intact until the end of the scene or the Dragon-Blood breaks commitment to that Charm, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> * shatter in place of the Willpower cost of a spell elementally associated with the blade, if the sorceress fails to have the Willpower refunded through success","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T23:56:12-07:00","id":1208743,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I <i>just</i> finished writing up mechanics for a 3 dot black jade reaper daiklave for my Single Point stylist. If any of you are interested, I'd be happy to post it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: ugh, this is what I get for posting while still half-asleep. I've misinterpreted the topic as &quot;ways for jade weapons in general to synergize with Single Point&quot; instead of &quot;here's this specific weapon idea, what stuff should it do&quot;. Disregard my shilling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifa